  "comment": "Multipath interference is a phenomenon in the physics of waves whereby a wave from a source travels to a detector via two or more paths and, under the right condition, the two (or more) components of the wave interfere . Multipath interference is a common cause of \" ghosting \" in analog television broadcasts. Conditions The condition necessary is that the components of the wave remain coherent",
